description_en:
20-16-20 mm nickel-plated brass transition tee—a reliable fitting for connecting pipes in central heating and water supply systems. It is used to branch off pipelines and connect pipes of different diameters in the utility systems of residential and commercial buildings.

The fitting is suitable for cross-linked polyethylene (PEX) and metal-plastic composite pipes, ensuring a strong and leak-proof connection for long-term use. The compression-type design allows for installation without welding, making the process more convenient and faster.

The nickel-plated brass body is highly durable and resistant to corrosion and temperature fluctuations. Thanks to its protective coating, the fitting is well-suited for hot and cold water supply systems, as well as heating circuits with constant load.

The 20-16-20 mm transition size allows for convenient piping layout and connection of various system sections.

Advantages of the transition tee:
suitable for PEX and metal-plastic pipes;
connection size 20-16-20 mm;
durable nickel-plated brass;
tight and reliable connection;
installation without welding;
resistance to corrosion and temperature fluctuations;
suitable for heating and water supply;
easy to install and maintain.

The 20-16-20 mm transition tee is a practical solution for creating a durable and reliable piping system in a house, apartment, or commercial space.

